+(duration-opts)=
+
+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a length of time into a
+{class}`datetime.timedelta`. The value is either a whole number of seconds,
+like `120`, or one or more groups of a whole number followed by a unit: `d`
+for days, `h` for hours, `m` for minutes and `s` for seconds. Each unit may
+appear at most once and in that order, without spaces, like `1h30m`, `90m` or
+`1d2h3m4s`. Units are case-insensitive. Negative numbers, decimals and other
+units are rejected.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s")
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting for {timeout}")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h30m'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=90'])
+    invoke(wait)
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1.5h'])
+```
+
